// ADR 0070 / register D44: a `Fn<T,R>`-typed CLASS field. The sibling of
// `c70_fn_field_in_struct.sentinel`, and the more important half of the pair.
//
// `scg`'s Pass-0 field renderer (`ll_type_to`) had no `cg_is_fn` arm, so a `Fn` field
// fell to the trailing `i64` in every aggregate it renders. In a class that gives
// `%Class.0 = type { i64, i64 }` against the oracle's `{ ptr, i64 }`.
//
// ⚠ THIS POSITION IS SILENT AND THE STRUCT ONE IS LOUD — that is why both exist.
// Measured on the pre-fix binary:
//   * struct field  → `llvm-as` REJECTS ("insertvalue operand and field disagree in
//     type: 'ptr' instead of 'i64'"), so the validity gate would have caught it;
//   * class field   → `llvm-as` is **CLEAN**. Storing a function pointer into an `i64`
//     slot assembles without a word, so the codegen differential's byte-COMPARE is the
//     ONLY thing in the harness that can see it. The two modules are even the same
//     LENGTH (943 bytes for the oracle, for pre-fix `scg` and for post-fix `scg`
//     alike), so a byte-COUNT check sees nothing either.
// A defect that is loud in one aggregate kind and silent in another is exactly the
// shape that survives a corpus sweep, and `ll_type_to` renders three of them (struct,
// class, generic instance) from one chain.
//
// The exit code is 42 either way — `snc build` goes through inkwell, which was always
// right. The pin is the differential.
//
// 40 + 2 = 42.
fn inc(x: i64) -> i64 { x + 1 }

class Holder {
    let f: Fn<i64, i64>;
    let n: i64;

    pub init(g: Fn<i64, i64>) {
        self.f = g;
        self.n = 40;
        0
    }

    pub fn read(self: &Self) -> i64 {
        self.n
    }
}

fn main() -> i64 {
    let h: Holder = Holder::init(inc);
    h.read() + 2
}
